## Toolchain

With [just](https://just.systems/man/en/packages.html) and [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/) installed:

```
just setup           # rustup with {{ t.rust_target }}, {{ tool_list }}{{ "; then `espup install && source ~/export-esp.sh`" if t.arch == "xtensa" else "" }}
just setup --check   # only report what is missing
```

`scripts/setup.py` runs on Arch, Ubuntu / Debian and Windows (winget) and skips what is already there. It prints
its plan first, naming each script it fetches from the internet and runs, the way these tools are meant to be
installed: probe-rs's udev rules file (pinned to a commit) and rustup's installer{{ "; probe-rs's installer, on Windows through `irm | iex` with `-ExecutionPolicy Bypass`" if probe_rs else "" }}. Steps that
need root or an administrator (system packages, the probe's udev rule{{ ", the " ~ probe[0] ~ " driver on Windows" if windows_driver else "" }}) are
printed for you; `just setup --root` runs them too, each shown first.
